- Saves JSON to file
- Includes export timestamp and result count

**Example:**
```python
from src import search, export

results = search.search("report")

# Return JSON string
json_str = export.export_json(results)
print(json_str)

# Save to file
export.export_json(results, output_path="results.json")

# Compact format
json_compact = export.export_json(results, pretty=False)
```

**JSON Structure:**
```json
{
  "exported_at": "2024-07-11T14:30:00.123456",
  "total_results": 42,
  "files": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "filename": "report.pdf",
      "path": "/path/to/report.pdf",
      "extension": ".pdf",
      "file_type": "document",
      "size": 2048576,
      "modified_date": "2024-06-15T10:30:00",
      ...
    }
  ]
}
